(x86_64-linux-gnu-gp-display-text) An alternate spelling for a command is shown in [], where applicable.

Those commands followed by a * may appear in .rc files.

Those commands followed by a $ can only appear in .rc files.

 
Commands controlling the function list:
     functions                                       display functions with current metrics
     metrics metric_spec                             set a new list of metrics
     sort metric_spec                                sort tables by the specified metric
     fsummary                                        display summary metrics for each function
     fsingle function_name #                         display the summary metrics for specified function
 
Commands controlling the callers-callees and calltree lists:
     callers-callees[gprof]                          display the callers-callees for each function
     csingle function_name #                         display the callers-callees for the specified function
     cprepend function_name #                        add specified function to the head of the callstack fragment
     cappend function_name #                         add specified function to the end of the callstack fragment
     crmfirst                                        remove the first function from the callstack fragment
     crmlast                                         remove the last function from the callstack fragment
     calltree[ctree]                                 display the tree of function calls
 
Commands controlling the leak and allocation lists:
     leaks                                           display memory leaks, aggregated by callstack
     allocs                                          display allocations, aggregated by callstack
     heap                                            display memory allocations and leaks, aggregated by callstack
     heapstat                                        display heap statistics report
 
Command controlling the I/O activity report:
     ioactivity                                      display I/O activity report, aggregated by file name
     iodetail                                        display I/O activity report, aggregated by file descriptor
     iocallstack                                     display I/O activity report, aggregated by callstack
     iostat                                          display I/O statistics report
 
Commands controlling the source and disassembly listings:
     pcs                                             display hot PC's with current metrics
     psummary                                        display summary metrics for each hot PC
     lines                                           display hot lines with current metrics
     lsummary                                        display summary metrics for each hot line
     source func/file #                              display annotated source for function/file
     disasm func/file #                              display annotated disassembly for function/file
     scc com_spec                                    set compiler commentary classes for source *
     sthresh value                                   set highlight threshold for source *
     dcc com_spec                                    set compiler commentary classes for disasm *
     cc com_spec                                     set compiler commentary classes for both source and disasm *
     dthresh value                                   set highlight threshold for disasm *
     setpath path_list                               set search path for annotated src/dis
     addpath path_list                               add search path for annotated src/dis *
     pathmap old_prefix new_prefix                   remap path prefix for annotated src/dis *
     preload_libdirs                                 remap path prefix for annotated src/dis *
 
Commands controlling the index objects:
     indxobj type                                    display index objects of a specified type with current metrics
     indxobj_list                                    display list of index objects
     indxobj_define type "index-expr"                define a new index object type *
 
Commands controlling the deadlock events lists:
     deadlocks                                       display deadlock events
     dsummary {deadlock_id|all}                      display summary for the deadlock event
 
Commands listing experiments, samples and threads:
     experiment_list[exp_list]                       display the existing experiments
     sample_list                                     display the list of existing samples
     lwp_list                                        display the list of existing LWPs
     thread_list                                     display the list of existing threads
     cpu_list                                        display the list of CPUs
 
Commands controlling filters:
     filters filter-specification                    define a filter
     describe                                        describe recorded data and tokens available for filtering data
 
Commands controlling old-style filters/selection:
     sample_select sample_spec                       set a new list of samples
     lwp_select lwp_spec                             set a new list of LWPs
     thread_select thread_spec                       set a new list of threads
     cpu_select cpu_spec                             set a new list of CPUs
 
Commands controlling load object selection:
     object_list                                     display load objects, functions-shown flag
     object_show obj1,...                            set load objects to show all functions *
     object_hide obj1,...                            set load objects to hide functions *
     object_api obj1,...                             set load objects to show API (entry point) only *
                                                       the special object name `all' refers to all load objects
     objects_default                                 reset load objects show to defaults
     object_select obj1,...                          set list of load objects whose functions are shown
 
Commands that list metrics:
     metric_list                                     display the available metrics and dmetrics keywords
     cmetric_list[gmetric_list]                      display the available callers-callees metrics
     indx_metric_list                                display the available index object metrics
 
Commands that control output:
     outfile filename                                open filename for subsequent output
     appendfile filename                             open filename for subsequent appended output
     limit n                                         limit output to the first n entries (n=0 for no limit)
     name {long|short|mangled}[:{soname|nosoname}]   set long/short/mangled names for functions *
     viewmode {user|expert|machine}                  set viewmode user|expert|machine *
     compare {on|off|delta|ratio}                    enable comparison mode for experiments *
     printmode string                                set the mode for printing tables *
 
Commands that print other displays:
     header exp_id                                   display information about the experiment
     objects                                         display object list with errors or warnings
     overview                                        display the overview of all loaded experiments
     sample_detail exp_id                            display the current sample list with data
     statistics exp_id                               display the execution statistics data
 
Commands for experiments (scripts and interactive mode only):
     open_exp experiment                             open experiment or group (drops all loaded experiments first)
     add_exp experiment                              add experiment or group
     drop_exp experiment                             drop experiment
 
Default-setting commands:
     dmetrics metric_spec                            set default function list metrics $
     dsort metric_spec                               set default function list sort metric $
     en_desc {on|off|=<regex>}                       enable descendant processes on|off|regex matches lineage or program name $
 
Default-setting commands that only affect gprofng GUI
     tlmode tl_mode                                  set default timeline mode, align, depth $
     tldata tl_data                                  set default timeline visible data $
     tabs tablist                                    set default visible tabs $
     callflame                                       request calltree flame chart -- not a command, but used in the tabs command
     timeline                                        request timeline -- not a command, but used in the tabs command
     dsrc                                            request dualsource tab -- not a command, but used in the tabs command
     srcdis                                          request source/disassembly tab -- not a command, but used in the tabs command
 
Miscellaneous commands:
     <type>                                          equivalent to "memobj type", or "indxobj type"
                                                       where type is a memory object or index object type
     ifreq                                           display instruction-frequency report
     procstats                                       display processing statistics
     script file                                     read er_print commands from script file
     version                                         display the current release version
     quit[exit]                                      terminate processing and exit
 
Help command:
     help                                            display the list of available commands
(x86_64-linux-gnu-gp-display-text) 